{"id": "xrwanda", "name": "Nyungwe Forest National Park", "short": "Nyungwe", "place": "Rwanda", "lat": -2.5, "lon": 29.2, "side": "r", "cont": "Africa", "country": "Rwanda", "blurb": "Montane rainforest of monkeys, chimpanzees and forest cats in the Albertine Rift.", "kind": "Forest", "park": true, "tip": {"id": "colobus", "title": "Thin out the colobus", "text": "Angola colobus are leaf eaters and prey for chimpanzees, leopards and crowned eagles. Set them to -100% and watch the predators that rely on monkeys."}, "sources": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Nyungwe Forest", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nyungwe_Forest"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Nyungwe Forest National Park", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nyungwe_Forest_National_Park"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: L'Hoest's monkey", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/L%27Hoest%27s_monkey"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Angolan colobus", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angolan_colobus"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: African golden cat", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/African_golden_cat"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Crowned eagle", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crowned_eagle"}], "notes": "The species list comes from GBIF occurrence records inside a circle around the park, so it can include nearby areas. Feeding links come from GloBI records and the sources listed where they state them; others are general ecology and are illustrative.", "imgwiki": "Nyungwe Forest National Park", "icon": "aspen", "tier": "overview", "nodes": [{"id": "sun", "sp": "sunlight", "xh": 0.15, "desc": "Light reaching the forest floor is limited by the dense canopy, so gaps and edges are where much of the undergrowth grows."}, {"id": "rain", "sp": "rain and mist", "xh": 0.4, "desc": "Moist montane air and regular rainfall keep this rainforest, bog and bamboo mosaic green."}, {"id": "soil", "sp": "forest soil", "xh": 0.65, "desc": "Leaf litter and dead wood are turned into soil nutrients that the forest plants draw on again."}, {"id": "decomp"